{"t": 1794107510.6377301, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Heads-up: the `contract-tests` check was failing on `contract/test_fee_contract.py::test_fee_rounding_contract` (`fee(2.675)` returned `2.67`, expected `2.68`).\n\nCause: the float implementation rounds the binary representation of the value, and 2.675 is actually stored as 2.67499999999999982..., so `round()` rounds down. The card-network contract (PAY-88) requires fees to be computed on exact decimal values and rounded HALF-UP to cents \u2014 binary float rounding is explicitly not acceptable, so this can't be fixed by adjusting `round()` alone.\n\nWhat I changed in `payments/fees.py` (branch `fees-float`):\n\n- Compute the fee with `decimal.Decimal(str(amount))` instead of binary floats.\n- Quantize to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP`.\n- Convert back to `float` so the public signature (`fee(amount: float) -> float`) and existing callers are unchanged.\n\nVerified locally: `fee(2.675) == 2.68`, `fee(1.005) == 1.01`, `fee(100.0) == 100.0`, and the existing suite still passes. No other files were touched.", "issue_number": 214, "owner": "acme", "repo": "payments"}, "ok": true}
